  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 1213 PM CDT Wed Aug 26 2026\n\nBehind the showers and storms Saturday morning, breezy conditions \nare expected due to a tight pressure gradient and strong flow at the \nlow levels. High pressure is still pancaking the Four Corners region \nleading to a broad upper level ridge and keeping Iowa in northwest \nflow through Saturday. Over the weekend the high is expected to \nweaken as the ridge is broken down by a potent trough that enters \nthe Pacific Northwest. This will end up leading to a pattern change \nwith warmer temperatures and more humid conditions through the end \nof the weekend and into next week. As the pattern changes, \nadditional storm chances are possible with any shortwave that rides \neastward across the broad upper-level ridge.",
